IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ta-nouns`
IMPORT `ta-logic`
IMPORT `ta-seat`

-- Terrorism Act 2000, Part III -- worked cases for the seat layer: at least one case per question, with the facts a real person in the seat would state,
-- and cases the Act does not answer.  Expected values are written from the text (the quoted words beside each case), never from what the code printed.
-- Calendar used below (2026): Mon 2 Nov; Wed 11 Nov; Thu 12 Nov; Sun 29 Nov; Mon 30 Nov; Mon 21 Dec; Fri 25 Dec (Christmas Day); Mon 28 Dec (the Boxing Day bank holiday); Fri 1 Jan 2027 (New Year's Day, a bank holiday); Mon 4 Jan 2027.

GIVETH A LIST OF DATE
`no bank holidays` MEANS EMPTY

GIVETH A LIST OF DATE
`28 December 2026 is a bank holiday` MEANS LIST (Date 28 12 2026)

GIVETH A LIST OF DATE
`28 December 2026 and 1 January 2027 are bank holidays` MEANS LIST (Date 28 12 2026), (Date 1 1 2027)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Is this money or other property terrorist property? (s 14)`
-- Inputs: likely to be used / for a proscribed organisation / proceeds of acts of terrorism / proceeds of acts carried out for the purposes of terrorism.
-- s 14(1)(a): "likely to be used for the purposes of terrorism (including any resources of a proscribed organisation)"
#ASSERT `Is this terrorist property` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 14(2)(b): the organisation's resources include money applied or made available for its use
#ASSERT `Is this terrorist property` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 14(1)(b), (c)
#ASSERT `Is this terrorist property` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is this terrorist property` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- none of the three limbs: "means" closes the definition, and s 14(2) extends only the two items it names, so the property is not terrorist property (fork F1, reading (a))
#ASSERT `Is this terrorist property` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 14(2)(a): "property which wholly or partly, and directly or indirectly, represents the proceeds of the act"; a payment or reward in connection with its commission
#ASSERT `Is this the proceeds of the act` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is this the proceeds of the act` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is this the proceeds of the act` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is this the proceeds of the act` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Do I commit an offence by what I do with money or other property? (ss 15 to 18 and 22)`
-- s 15(1) inputs: invited / intended / reasonable cause to suspect it will or may be used
#ASSERT `Do I commit an offence by inviting` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Do I commit an offence by inviting` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- invited, but neither intending nor having reasonable cause to suspect: the text's "if" is not met
#ASSERT `Do I commit an offence by inviting` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- no invitation at all
#ASSERT `Do I commit an offence by inviting` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 15(2) inputs: received / intended / reasonable cause to suspect it may be used
#ASSERT `Do I commit an offence by receiving` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Do I commit an offence by receiving` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 15(3) with s 15(4) inputs: gave / lent / otherwise made available / for consideration / knew it would be used / reasonable cause to suspect it will or may be used
#ASSERT `Do I commit an offence by providing` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 15(4): to provide is to give, lend or otherwise make available "whether or not for consideration"
#ASSERT `Do I commit an offence by providing` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Do I commit an offence by providing` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Do I commit an offence by providing` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 16(1) input: used it for the purposes of terrorism
#ASSERT `Do I commit an offence by using` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Do I commit an offence by using` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 16(2) inputs: possess / intend / reasonable cause to suspect it may be used
#ASSERT `Do I commit an offence by possessing` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Do I commit an offence by possessing` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Do I commit an offence by possessing` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Do I commit an offence by possessing` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 17 inputs: entered / became concerned / money made available to another / knew it would be used / reasonable cause to suspect it will or may be used
#ASSERT `Do I commit an offence by a funding arrangement` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Do I commit an offence by a funding arrangement` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Do I commit an offence by a funding arrangement` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Do I commit an offence by a funding arrangement` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 17A(1) inputs: insurer / paid under the contract / in respect of property handed over to a terrorist demand / insurer knew or suspected / the authoriser knew or suspected
#ASSERT `Do I commit an offence as an insurer` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Do I commit an offence as an insurer` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Do I commit an offence as an insurer` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Do I commit an offence as an insurer` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 18(1) inputs: entered / became concerned / by concealment / by removal / by nominees / any other way / likely to be used / for a proscribed organisation / proceeds of terrorism / proceeds of acts for terrorism
#ASSERT `Do I commit an offence by a laundering arrangement` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Do I commit an offence by a laundering arrangement` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- no arrangement
#ASSERT `Do I commit an offence by a laundering arrangement` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the property is not terrorist property under any limb of s 14(1), which "means" the three limbs: the last element of s 18(1) is missing (fork F1, reading (a))
#ASSERT `Do I commit an offence by a laundering arrangement` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 18(2) inputs: charged under s 18(1) / prove I did not know / prove I had no reasonable cause to suspect
-- ruling of 2026-11-05 (b): a proof not made leaves no defence under THIS section on these facts (JUST FALSE, not "no defence at all"); a person not charged under s 18(1) is outside the grant (scope, ruling (c)): NOTHING
#ASSERT `Do I have a defence under s 18(2)` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Do I have a defence under s 18(2)` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Do I have a defence under s 18(2)` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Do I have a defence under s 18(2)` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 22: 14 years is 168 months; four thousand is a test input for the statutory maximum, not the Act's figure
#ASSERT `What is the highest penalty for ss 15 to 18` `on conviction on indictment` 4000 EQUALS `Penalty ceiling` OF 168, `No ceiling is stated`
#ASSERT `What is the highest penalty for ss 15 to 18` `on summary conviction` 4000 EQUALS `Penalty ceiling` OF 6, `A fine not exceeding` 4000

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Telling the police: must I, may I, am I protected? (ss 19 to 21ZC)`
-- s 19(1) inputs: believe or suspect an offence under ss 15 to 18 / from a trade, profession or business / from employment
#ASSERT `Does section 19 apply to me` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does section 19 apply to me` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does section 19 apply to me` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does section 19 apply to me` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 19(1A) input: the information came in the course of a business in the regulated sector
#ASSERT `Is section 19 switched off` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is section 19 switched off` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 19(2) inputs: believe or suspect / trade / employment / regulated sector / told the belief / told the information / as soon as reasonably practicable
#ASSERT `Do I commit an offence under s 19(2)` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Do I commit an offence under s 19(2)` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- told the belief but not the information on which it is based: not having disclosed "(a) his belief or suspicion, and (b) the information" (fork F2)
#ASSERT `Do I commit an offence under s 19(2)` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- section 19 does not apply, so there is no offence under it
#ASSERT `Do I commit an offence under s 19(2)` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 19(1A): "this section does not apply if the information came to the person in the course of a business in the regulated sector"
#ASSERT `Do I commit an offence under s 19(2)` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 19(3) inputs: charged under s 19(2) / prove a reasonable excuse
#ASSERT `Do I have a defence under s 19(3)` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Do I have a defence under s 19(3)` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Do I have a defence under s 19(3)` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 19(4) inputs: in employment / employer established a procedure / charged / disclosed under the procedure
#ASSERT `Do I have a defence under s 19(4)` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Do I have a defence under s 19(4)` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Do I have a defence under s 19(4)` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 19(5) inputs: professional legal adviser / information in privileged circumstances / belief based on such information
#ASSERT `Does section 19(2) require me to disclose` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does section 19(2) require me to disclose` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does section 19(2) require me to disclose` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Does section 19(2) require me to disclose` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 20(1) inputs: a suspicion or belief about terrorist property / a matter on which it is based / told to a constable
#ASSERT `May I tell a constable` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `May I tell a constable` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a disclosure to someone other than a constable is outside the permission
#ASSERT `May I tell a constable` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 21(1)
#ASSERT `Do I avoid an offence by consent` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Do I avoid an offence by consent` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 21(2) to (4) inputs: involved / told the suspicion / told the information / after becoming concerned / own initiative / as soon as reasonably practicable / a constable forbade / I continued
#ASSERT `Do I avoid an offence by telling a constable` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 21(4): a constable forbade it and I carried on, so subsection (2) does not apply
#ASSERT `Do I avoid an offence by telling a constable` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- told but not on my own initiative
#ASSERT `Do I avoid an offence by telling a constable` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 21(5) inputs: the offence charged / intended to make a disclosure / reasonable excuse for not having done so
#ASSERT `Do I have a defence under s 21(5)` `an offence under s 15(2)` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 21(5) names "sections 15(2) and (3) and 16 to 18": section 15(1) is not named
#ASSERT `Do I have a defence under s 21(5)` `an offence under s 15(1)` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Do I have a defence under s 21(5)` `an offence under s 18` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Do I have a defence under s 21(5)` `an offence under s 18` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 21ZA(1) inputs: involved / disclosed to an authorised officer before becoming involved / have the officer's consent
#ASSERT `Do I avoid an offence by prior consent` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Do I avoid an offence by prior consent` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 21ZA(3): seven working days after the first working day after the disclosure.  Disclosed Mon 2 Nov: Tue 3 (1), Wed 4 (2), Thu 5 (3), Fri 6 (4), Mon 9 (5), Tue 10 (6), Wed 11 (7)
#ASSERT `On what day does the notice period end` (Date 2 11 2026) `no bank holidays` EQUALS Date 11 11 2026
-- Disclosed Mon 21 Dec with Christmas Day Fri 25 Dec, Mon 28 Dec and Fri 1 Jan bank holidays: Tue 22 (1), Wed 23 (2), Thu 24 (3), Tue 29 (4), Wed 30 (5), Thu 31 (6), Mon 4 Jan (7)
#ASSERT `On what day does the notice period end` (Date 21 12 2026) `28 December 2026 and 1 January 2027 are bank holidays` EQUALS Date 4 1 2027
-- The same disclosure with a list that omits 1 January: the answer follows the list the person gives (fork F4), so Fri 1 Jan counts as the 7th working day
#ASSERT `On what day does the notice period end` (Date 21 12 2026) `28 December 2026 is a bank holiday` EQUALS Date 1 1 2027
-- s 21ZA(2) inputs: day disclosed / bank holidays / received notice of refusal / the day received / the day I am asking about
-- no notice, asked on the day after the period ended (Wed 11 Nov): treated as having consent
#ASSERT `Am I treated as having consent` (Date 2 11 2026) `no bank holidays` FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 12 11 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- no notice, asked on the last day: the period has not ended, so the "if before the end of the notice period" is not met: JUST FALSE (ruling of 2026-11-05, (a); fork F3)
#ASSERT `Am I treated as having consent` (Date 2 11 2026) `no bank holidays` FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 11 11 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- notice of refusal received Thu 5 Nov, inside the period
#ASSERT `Am I treated as having consent` (Date 2 11 2026) `no bank holidays` TRUE (Date 5 11 2026) (Date 20 11 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- notice of refusal received Thu 12 Nov, after the period ended
#ASSERT `Am I treated as having consent` (Date 2 11 2026) `no bank holidays` TRUE (Date 12 11 2026) (Date 20 11 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 21ZB(1) to (3) inputs: involved / disclosed afterwards / reasonable excuse for not disclosing before / own initiative / as soon as reasonably practicable / authorised officer forbade / I continued
#ASSERT `Do I avoid an offence by a later disclosure` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Do I avoid an offence by a later disclosure` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Do I avoid an offence by a later disclosure` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 21ZC inputs: charged under ss 15 to 18 / prove I intended to disclose / prove a reasonable excuse
#ASSERT `Do I have a defence under s 21ZC` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Do I have a defence under s 21ZC` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Do I have a defence under s 21ZC` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Do I have a defence under s 21ZC` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `A business in the regulated sector: what must I disclose, to whom and when? (ss 21A to 21C)`
-- s 21A inputs: know or suspect / reasonable grounds / information came in the regulated sector / disclosed as soon as practicable / reasonable excuse / adviser / privileged / assistant / in connection / came to the adviser in privileged circumstances
#ASSERT `Do I commit an offence under s 21A` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Do I commit an offence under s 21A` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 21A(4): the third condition is that the person does not disclose as soon as practicable; here the person did
#ASSERT `Do I commit an offence under s 21A` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 21A(5)(a): a reasonable excuse
#ASSERT `Do I commit an offence under s 21A` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 21A(5)(b): a legal adviser holding the information in privileged circumstances
#ASSERT `Do I commit an offence under s 21A` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 21A(5A): an assistant to such an adviser
#ASSERT `Do I commit an offence under s 21A` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- no knowledge or suspicion, and no reasonable grounds
#ASSERT `Do I commit an offence under s 21A` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- information that did not come in the regulated sector
#ASSERT `Do I commit an offence under s 21A` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- What must I tell (inputs): know or suspect / reasonable grounds / regulated sector (Yes, No, I am not sure) / trade, profession or business / employment / reasonable excuse / adviser (legal or professional) / privileged / assistant / in connection / came to the adviser in privileged circumstances / professional legal adviser
#ASSERT `What must I tell and to whom` TRUE FALSE Yes FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `to a constable or a nominated officer as soon as is practicable (s 21A(4))`
#ASSERT `What must I tell and to whom` TRUE FALSE No TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `to a constable as soon as is reasonably practicable (s 19(2))`
#ASSERT `What must I tell and to whom` TRUE FALSE No FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `to a constable as soon as is reasonably practicable (s 19(2))`
-- s 19(1): the belief did not come from a trade, profession, business or employment
#ASSERT `What must I tell and to whom` TRUE FALSE No FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not obliged under s 19 or s 21A`
-- s 21A(5)(a): a reasonable excuse
#ASSERT `What must I tell and to whom` TRUE FALSE Yes FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not obliged under s 19 or s 21A`
-- s 21A(2): no knowledge, suspicion or reasonable grounds
#ASSERT `What must I tell and to whom` FALSE FALSE Yes FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not obliged under s 19 or s 21A`
-- s 19(5): a professional legal adviser holding the information in privileged circumstances is not required to disclose
#ASSERT `What must I tell and to whom` TRUE FALSE No TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `not obliged under s 19 or s 21A`
-- whether the information came in the regulated sector turns on Schedule 3A; the person is not sure
#ASSERT `What must I tell and to whom` TRUE FALSE `I am not sure` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the Act does not answer on these facts`
-- s 21B inputs: information came in the regulated sector / caused me to know or suspect / gave reasonable grounds / made to a constable or nominated officer / as soon as practicable
#ASSERT `Is my disclosure protected` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my disclosure protected` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a disclosure that misses the third condition is outside "A disclosure which satisfies the following three conditions": JUST FALSE (fork F17)
#ASSERT `Is my disclosure protected` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 21A(15) inputs: accountant, auditor or tax adviser / member of a professional body / the body tests competence / the body sets standards and sanctions
#ASSERT `Am I a relevant professional adviser` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I a relevant professional adviser` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Passing information to another business in the regulated sector (ss 21CA to 21CF)`
-- s 21CA(1) inputs: a relevant undertaking / information came in that business / each recipient a relevant undertaking / a constable asked / a recipient asked / required notification made / assists a suspicion / assists identification / the requester notified a constable
-- a constable asked: condition 5 does not apply (s 21CA(7))
#ASSERT `May I disclose under s 21CA` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a recipient asked and the requester notified a constable (condition 5)
#ASSERT `May I disclose under s 21CA` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a recipient asked and the requester did not notify a constable: condition 5 fails, so the "if" in s 21CA(1) is not met: JUST FALSE (ruling of 2026-11-05)
#ASSERT `May I disclose under s 21CA` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the required notification has not been made (condition 3): the "if" is not met, JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `May I disclose under s 21CA` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 21CC(2) inputs: made the required notification / in good faith
#ASSERT `Does my notification satisfy the duty` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does my notification satisfy the duty` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 21CC(7) and (8) inputs: who asked / the day of the notification / a constable varied the 28 days by written notice / the new length / a constable set a period / the last day of it
-- a recipient asked: 28 days beginning with Mon 2 Nov end on Sun 29 Nov
#ASSERT `By what day must the report be sent` `a person mentioned in s 21CA(3)(b)` (Date 2 11 2026) FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) EQUALS JUST (Date 29 11 2026)
-- shortened to 14 days by written notice: Sun 15 Nov
#ASSERT `By what day must the report be sent` `a person mentioned in s 21CA(3)(b)` (Date 2 11 2026) TRUE FALSE 14 FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) EQUALS JUST (Date 15 11 2026)
-- a constable asked and set a period ending Fri 20 Nov
#ASSERT `By what day must the report be sent` `a constable` (Date 2 11 2026) FALSE FALSE 0 TRUE (Date 20 11 2026) EQUALS JUST (Date 20 11 2026)
-- a constable asked and set no period: the Act points to a period it does not state
#ASSERT `By what day must the report be sent` `a constable` (Date 2 11 2026) FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
-- a constable gave notice of a different period that was not in writing: s 21CC(8) gives the power "by giving written notice" and says nothing of another notice, so the end date is not answered
#ASSERT `By what day must the report be sent` `a person mentioned in s 21CA(3)(b)` (Date 2 11 2026) FALSE TRUE 0 FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 21CC(4)(d) inputs: the day sent / who asked / day of notification / varied / new length / a constable set a period / its last day
#ASSERT `Was my report sent in time` (Date 29 11 2026) `a person mentioned in s 21CA(3)(b)` (Date 2 11 2026) FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Was my report sent in time` (Date 30 11 2026) `a person mentioned in s 21CA(3)(b)` (Date 2 11 2026) FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Was my report sent in time` (Date 30 11 2026) `a constable` (Date 2 11 2026) FALSE FALSE 0 FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
-- the same with a notice of a different period that was not in writing: not answered
#ASSERT `Was my report sent in time` (Date 30 11 2026) `a person mentioned in s 21CA(3)(b)` (Date 2 11 2026) FALSE TRUE 0 FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 21CD(9)
#ASSERT `Must I notify that no report is being made` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Must I notify that no report is being made` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 21CE(2) inputs: the information came from a UK law enforcement agency / that agency consents
#ASSERT `Am I barred from including that information` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I barred from including that information` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I barred from including that information` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Telling someone else: do I commit the offence of tipping off, and is my disclosure excused? (ss 21D to 21G)`
-- s 21D(1) inputs: a disclosure was made / to a constable / per the employer's procedure / to a nominated officer / to an NCA officer / of information from the regulated sector / likely to prejudice an investigation / the information I would tell came in the regulated sector
#ASSERT `Do I commit the offence of tipping off` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Do I commit the offence of tipping off` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- no recognised route for the disclosure, so it is not a matter within s 21D(2)
#ASSERT `Do I commit the offence of tipping off` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- not likely to prejudice an investigation
#ASSERT `Do I commit the offence of tipping off` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 21D(3) inputs: disclose that an investigation is contemplated or carried out / likely to prejudice it / the information came in the regulated sector
#ASSERT `Do I commit an offence by disclosing an investigation` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Do I commit an offence by disclosing an investigation` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 21E(1) inputs: employee, officer or partner / the disclosure is to one in the same undertaking
#ASSERT `Am I excused by s 21E(1)` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I excused by s 21E(1)` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 21E(2) inputs: by a credit or financial institution / to one / recipient in the UK, an EEA state or an equivalent country / same group
#ASSERT `Am I excused by s 21E(2)` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I excused by s 21E(2)` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 21F inputs: credit to credit / financial to financial / legal adviser to legal adviser / professional adviser to one of the same kind / client / transaction / service / purpose only / recipient situated / equivalent duties
#ASSERT `Am I excused by s 21F` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 21F(1): the disclosure is between none of the listed pairs, so s 21F does not apply
#ASSERT `Am I excused by s 21F` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 21F(2)(a): relates to no shared client, transaction or service
#ASSERT `Am I excused by s 21F` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 21G(1) inputs: to my supervisory authority / in good faith under s 21CA / to detect, investigate or prosecute an offence / for a Proceeds of Crime Act investigation / to enforce a court order under that Act
#ASSERT `Am I excused by s 21G(1)` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I excused by s 21G(1)` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 21G(2) inputs: legal or professional adviser / disclosure to my client / to dissuade the client from conduct amounting to an offence
#ASSERT `Am I excused by s 21G(2)` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I excused by s 21G(2)` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 21G(3): "does not know or suspect that the disclosure is likely to have the effect"
#ASSERT `Am I excused by s 21G(3)` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I excused by s 21G(3)` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Being ordered to hand over information (ss 22B to 22F)`
-- s 22B(4) inputs: arises from a s 21A disclosure / I made it / I otherwise carry on a business in the regulated sector / assists an investigation / assists identifying terrorist property / reasonable
#ASSERT `Is condition 1 met against me` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is condition 1 met against me` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is condition 1 met against me` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 22B(3) inputs: specified in the application / the court thinks it appropriate / in my possession or under my control
#ASSERT `Does the order require me to provide it` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does the order require me to provide it` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 22B(8) inputs: failed to comply / the order was made by a magistrates court
#ASSERT `May the court order me to pay` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `May the court order me to pay` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 22B(8): "an amount not exceeding £5,000", unless regulations have substituted another sum
#ASSERT `What is the most I may be ordered to pay` FALSE 0 EQUALS 5000
#ASSERT `What is the most I may be ordered to pay` TRUE 7500 EQUALS 7500
-- s 22E(1) inputs: entitled to refuse on legal professional privilege in High Court proceedings / in Scotland, legal privilege under s 412
#ASSERT `Does the order give a right to require it` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does the order give a right to require it` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does the order give a right to require it` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Does providing it breach a restriction` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does providing it breach a restriction` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 22C(1) inputs: a statement made in response to an information order / it would be used in criminal proceedings against me
#ASSERT `Is my statement barred from use against me` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my statement barred from use against me` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 22D(3)
#ASSERT `To which court do I appeal` `a magistrates court in England and Wales` EQUALS `the Crown Court`
#ASSERT `To which court do I appeal` `a magistrates court in Northern Ireland` EQUALS `a county court`
#ASSERT `To which court do I appeal` `the sheriff` EQUALS `the Sheriff Appeal Court`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Forfeiture of property after a conviction (ss 23 to 23B)`
-- inputs: the offence / in my possession or control / had been used / I intended it / reasonable cause to suspect it might be used / knew or had reasonable cause to suspect it would or might be used / the arrangement related to it / a payment or reward / the insured amount
-- s 23(2): s 16(1) offence, property in my possession and used
#ASSERT `Could the court order forfeiture` `an offence under s 16(1)` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 23(3): s 15(3) offence, property in my possession and known or suspected to be about to be used
#ASSERT `Could the court order forfeiture` `an offence under s 15(3)` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 23(4): s 17 offence, intended
#ASSERT `Could the court order forfeiture` `an offence under s 17` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 23(6): s 18 offence, the arrangement's property
#ASSERT `Could the court order forfeiture` `an offence under s 18` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 23(5A): s 17A offence, the amount paid under the contract
#ASSERT `Could the court order forfeiture` `an offence under s 17A` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 23(7): a payment or reward, for any offence under ss 15 to 18
#ASSERT `Could the court order forfeiture` `an offence under s 15(1)` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 15(3) offence, the property held and intended but not known or suspected to be about to be used and not used: no subsection gives the power; the Act does not say the court may not
#ASSERT `Could the court order forfeiture` `an offence under s 15(3)` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 23B(1) inputs: the court is about to make an order / I am the convicted person / I claim to be the owner or otherwise interested
#ASSERT `Must the court hear me` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "other than the convicted person"
#ASSERT `Must the court hear me` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Must the court hear me` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- 181 assertions written; 181 satisfied (run with l4 1.6.109 on the main build; check.sh recounts)
